From: Ze kernel maintainers
Subject: [PATCH 13da] ppp: refuse control construction from a foreign namespace

PRIVATE SOURCE ONLY after the exact complete Source13 set and 0013d.
Mirror the original-unit probe's current network namespace check before
capability checks, logical owner acquisition or socket creation. A creator
file retained across setns must not create a socket in its former namespace.
All frozen predecessors remain unchanged. No native acceptance is claimed.

--- a/drivers/net/ppp/ppp_generic.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ppp/ppp_generic.c
@@ -1510,6 +1510,10 @@
 	if (ppp->control_retired || ppp_validate_owner(dev, file) ||
 	    request.unit != pf->index || request.ifindex != dev->ifindex)
 		goto unlock;
+	if (!net_eq(dev_net(dev), current->nsproxy->net_ns)) {
+		err = -EXDEV;
+		goto unlock;
+	}
 	if (!ns_capable(dev_net(dev)->user_ns, CAP_NET_ADMIN)) {
 		err = -EPERM;
 		goto unlock;
